er 24\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Cisco uses \"l2vpn xconnect context\" to create a similar pseudowire template\\n2. The peer address is specified with \"encapsulation mpls\"\\n3. The jitter buffer and TDM encapsulation parameters remain similar\\n4. The VC ID (100/200 from the original) would be specified when applying this template to an interface in Cisco, not in the template itself', 'trans_template': 'jitter-buffer depth 8'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tdm-encapsulation number 24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'tdm-encapsulation number 24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent for the `pw-template` command:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context 1to3\\n peer 192.168.3.3 encapsulation mpls\\n jitter-buffer depth 8\\n tdm-encapsulation number 24\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Cisco uses \"l2vpn xconnect context\" to create a similar pseudowire template\\n2. The peer address is specified with \"encapsulation mpls\"\\n3. The jitter buffer and TDM encapsulation parameters remain similar\\n4. The VC ID (100/200 from the original) would be specified when applying this template to an interface in Cisco, not in the template itself', 'trans_template': 'tdm-encapsulation number 24'}]]": 1,
