    "['using ce1', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'controller E1 1/0/1', 'parent_command': ['controller E1 [parameter1]'], 'root': 'controller E1 [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ncontroller E1 1/0/1\\n framing crc4\\n channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `using ce1` command specifies that the E1 controller operates in CE1 (Channelized E1) mode. In Cisco, this is the default mode for E1 controllers, so no direct equivalent command is needed. However, the complete Cisco equivalent configuration for the E1 controller section includes the `framing` and `channel-group` commands, which are necessary for proper operation (similar to Huawei's `frame-format` and `channel-set` commands).\", 'trans_template': 'controller E1 1/0/1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'framing crc4', 'parent_command': ['controller E1 [parameter1]'], 'root': 'controller E1 [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ncontroller E1 1/0/1\\n framing crc4\\n channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `using ce1` command specifies that the E1 controller operates in CE1 (Channelized E1) mode. In Cisco, this is the default mode for E1 controllers, so no direct equivalent command is needed. However, the complete Cisco equivalent configuration for the E1 controller section includes the `framing` and `channel-group` commands, which are necessary for proper operation (similar to Huawei's `frame-format` and `channel-set` commands).\", 'trans_template': 'framing crc4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': ['controller E1 [parameter1]'], 'root': 'controller E1 [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ncontroller E1 1/0/1\\n framing crc4\\n channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `using ce1` command specifies that the E1 controller operates in CE1 (Channelized E1) mode. In Cisco, this is the default mode for E1 controllers, so no direct equivalent command is needed. However, the complete Cisco equivalent configuration for the E1 controller section includes the `framing` and `channel-group` commands, which are necessary for proper operation (similar to Huawei's `frame-format` and `channel-set` commands).\", 'trans_template': 'channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31'}]]": 1,
    "['frame-format [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'framing crc4', 'parent_command': ['controller E1 [parameter1]'], 'root': 'controller E1 [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nframing crc4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: \\nIn Huawei's configuration, `frame-format crc4` sets the E1 framing format to CRC4. The equivalent Cisco command is `framing crc4`, which performs the same function of configuring CRC4 framing for E1 controllers.\", 'trans_template': 'framing crc4'}]]": 1,
